hadiths[15]{hadithnumber,text}:
"24202","Yazid narrated to us, al-Walid, meaning Ibn Abdillah ibn Jumay', informed us, from Abu al-Tufayl, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came back from the expedition of Tabuk, he ordered a crier who called out: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has taken the mountain pass, so let no one take it. And while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was being led by Hudhayfah and driven by Ammar, a group of veiled men on mounts came, crowding Ammar while he was driving the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and Ammar began striking the faces of the mounts. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Hudhayfah: Drive on, drive on, until the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) descended. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) descended he alighted, and Ammar returned. So he said: O Ammar, did you recognize the people? He said: I recognized most of the mounts, while the people were veiled. He said: Do you know what they intended? He said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: They intended to make the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) shy away so as to throw him. He said: So Ammar asked a man from among the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I adjure you by Allah, how many do you know the companions of the pass were? He said: Fourteen. So he said: If you were among them, then they were fifteen. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) named three of them. They said: By Allah, we did not hear the crier of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), nor did we know what the people intended. So Ammar said: I bear witness that the remaining twelve are at war with Allah and His Messenger in the life of this world and on the day the witnesses will stand. Al-Walid said: And Abu al-Tufayl mentioned regarding that expedition that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to the people, and it was mentioned to him that water was scarce, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered a crier who called out that no one should come to the water before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to it and found a group who had come to it before him, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed them on that day."
"24203","Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me from his book, Ibrahim ibn Khalid narrated to us, Rabah ibn Zayd narrated to us, Umar ibn Habib narrated to me, from Abdullah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym, who said: I entered upon Abu al-Tufayl and found him in good spirits, so I said: I shall take advantage of that from him. So I said: O Abu al-Tufayl, the group whom the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed, who are they among them? So he was about to inform me of them, but a black woman said to him: Hush, O Abu al-Tufayl, has it not reached you that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, I am only a human, so whichever servant among the believers I supplicate against with a supplication, make it for him purification and mercy."
"24204","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym, from Abu al-Tufayl, who said: When the House was built, the people were carrying stones while the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was carrying with them. So he took his garment and placed it on his shoulder, and he was called out to: Do not uncover your private part. So he threw the stone and wore his garment, (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"24205","Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Hammad, meaning Ibn Zayd, narrated to us, Uthman ibn Ubayd al-Rasibi narrated to us, who said: I heard Abu al-Tufayl say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no prophethood after me except the heralds of glad tidings. He said: It was said: And what are the heralds of glad tidings, O Messenger of Allah? He said: The good dream, or he said: The righteous dream."
"24206","Abu Sa'id, freedman of Banu Hashim, narrated to us, Mahdi ibn Imran al-Mazini narrated to us, who said: I heard Abu al-Tufayl, and he was asked: Did you see the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Yes. It was said: Did you speak to him? He said: No, but I saw him set out to such-and-such place, with Abdullah ibn Mas'ud and some of his companions with him, until he came to the house of Qawra'. So he said: Open this door. So it was opened, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered, and I entered with him, and there was a velvet cloth in the middle of the house. So he said: Lift this velvet cloth. So they lifted the velvet cloth, and there was a one-eyed boy under the velvet cloth. So he said: Stand, O boy. So the boy stood. So he said: O boy, do you bear witness that I am the Messenger of Allah? The boy said: Do you bear witness that I am the Messenger of Allah? He said: Do you bear witness that I am the Messenger of Allah? The boy said: Do you bear witness that I am the Messenger of Allah? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Seek refuge with Allah from the evil of this, twice."
"24207","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, al-Jurayri informed us, who said: I was circumambulating with Abu al-Tufayl, and he said: No one remains who saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except me. He said: I said: And you saw him? He said: Yes. He said: I said: How was his description? He said: He was white, handsome, moderate in stature."
"24208","Waki' narrated to us, Ma'ruf al-Makki narrated to us, who said: I heard Abu al-Tufayl Amir ibn Wathilah say: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when I was a young lad, circumambulating the House on his mount, touching the Stone with his crooked staff."
"24209","Thabit ibn al-Walid ibn Abdillah ibn Jumay' narrated to us, my father narrated to me, who said: Abu al-Tufayl said to me: I lived through eight years of the life of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I was born in the year of Uhud."
"24210","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar informed us, from Ibn Khuthaym, from Abu al-Tufayl, and he mentioned the building of the Ka'bah in the pre-Islamic period, who said: Quraysh demolished it and began building it with stones of the valley, with Quraysh carrying them on their necks. So they raised it into the sky twenty cubits. And while the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was carrying stones from Ajyad with a striped cloak on him, the cloak became tight on him, so he went to place the cloak on his shoulder so that his private part would be seen because of the smallness of the cloak. So he was called out to: O Muhammad, cover your private part. So he was never seen naked after that."
"24211","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Ali ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Abu al-Tufayl, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I saw in what the sleeper sees as though I were drawing from a land, and black sheep and dusty-white sheep came to me. So Abu Bakr came and drew a bucket or two buckets, and in them was weakness, and Allah forgives him. Then Umar came and drew, and it turned into a large bucket, so he filled the basin and watered the arrivals. So I have never seen a genius drawing better than Umar. So I interpreted that the black ones are the Arabs and that the dusty-white ones are the non-Arabs."
"24212","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Abdullah Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Abi Ziyad, who said: I heard Abu al-Tufayl narrate that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) walked briskly from the Stone to the Stone."
"24213","Abu Kamil Muzaffar ibn Mudrik narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated to us, Ibn Shihab narrated to us, from Abu al-Tufayl Amir ibn Wathilah, that a man passed by some people and greeted them, and they returned the greeting to him. When he passed them, a man among them said: By Allah, I hate this man for the sake of Allah. So the people of the sitting said: By Allah, evil is what you have said. By Allah, we shall surely inform him. Stand, O so-and-so, a man among them, and inform him. He said: So their messenger caught up with him and informed him of what he said. So the man turned back until he came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I passed by a sitting of Muslims among whom was so-and-so, and I greeted them, and they returned the greeting. When I passed them, a man among them caught up with me and informed me that so-and-so said: By Allah, I hate this man for the sake of Allah, so call him and ask him for what he hates me. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called him. So he asked him about what the man had told him, and he admitted it and said: I did say that to him, O Messenger of Allah. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: So why do you hate him? He said: I am his neighbor and I know him well. By Allah, I have never seen him pray any prayer at all except this prescribed prayer which the righteous and the wicked pray. The man said: Ask him, O Messenger of Allah, did he ever see me delay it past its time, or perform ablution for it badly, or perform bowing and prostration in it badly? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked him about that, and he said: No. Then he said: By Allah, I have never seen him fast at all except this month which the righteous and the wicked fast. He said: O Messenger of Allah, did he ever see me break fast in it or fall short in any of its right? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked him, and he said: No. Then he said: By Allah, I have never seen him give a beggar anything at all, nor have I seen him spend any of his wealth in anything of the path of Allah for good except this charity which the righteous and the wicked give. He said: So ask him, O Messenger of Allah, did I ever conceal any of the zakah at all or bargain with its seeker? He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked him about that, and he said: No. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Stand; I do not know, perhaps he is better than you."
"24214","Ya'qub narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, that he informed him that a man during the life of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by some people, and he did not mention Abu al-Tufayl. Abdullah said: It reached me that Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated this hadith from his memory and said: From Abu al-Tufayl. His son Ya'qub narrated it from his father and did not mention Abu al-Tufayl, so I think he erred, and the correct is the narration of Ya'qub, and Allah knows best."
"24215","Yunus and Affan narrated to us, both saying: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Abu al-Tufayl, that a boy was born to a man at the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who took the skin of his face and supplicated for blessing for him. He said: So a hair grew on his forehead like the shape of a bow, and the boy grew up. When the time of the Khawarij came, he loved them, so the hair fell from his forehead. So his father took him and shackled him and imprisoned him, fearing he would join them. He said: So we entered upon him and admonished him, and we said to him among what we said: Have you not seen that the blessing of the supplication of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has fallen from your forehead? So we kept at him until he turned back from their view, and Allah returned the hair to his forehead afterwards, and he repented."
"24216","Ya'mar ibn Bishr narrated to us, Abdullah, meaning Ibn Mubarak, narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Abi Ziyad narrated to us, who said: I heard Abu al-Tufayl say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) walked briskly three times from the Stone to the Stone."
